| $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $2$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n| $y$ | $7$ | $12$ | $11$ | {{field-2}} | $39$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $x={t}^{2}-2t+2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(1)=(1)^{2}-2(1)+2=1-2+2=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=2(2)^{3}-3(2)^{2}+12=16-12+12=16.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+12.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(4)=2(4)^{3}-3(4)^{2}+12=128-48+12=92.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n| $y$ | $7$ | $12$ | $11$ | $16$ | $39$ | $92$ |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2f74f3-79cd-574f-9238-6fcdf77522bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b2f74f3-79cd-574f-9238-6fcdf77522bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299987} :answer-field/id #uuid "27b250f4-4f05-544b-8ebc-03ff71447626" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf5af01e-616b-5c46-a431-35738aad2c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf5af01e-616b-5c46-a431-35738aad2c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300920} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf8b63ee-6e28-54cd-8eb2-72e238c6f9eb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301894} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "521f8156-1852-5b70-b978-7d31f5f9d99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{121}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521f8156-1852-5b70-b978-7d31f5f9d99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{121}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300388} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec5a0f5f-9550-5151-a6a5-e2b91e74b30c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8c7b5c0-57d6-5e10-9424-b187294f0724" :question/math-academy-id "q-326250" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2,\\,y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1},\\,0\\le t\\le 5.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3}-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(5)=\\frac{1}{2}(5)^{3}-2=\\frac{125}{2}-\\frac{4}{2}=\\frac{121}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{2-1}{2+1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(5),$ we substitute $t=5$ into $y=\\frac{t-1}{t+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(0)=\\frac{5-1}{5+1}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ | $2$ | $\\frac{23}{2}$ | $30$ | $\\frac{121}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302273 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dea4c418-a2a3-5eb1-914f-abfb1e44f530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dea4c418-a2a3-5eb1-914f-abfb1e44f530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301065} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f6a1cf6-f1e9-5324-a0cd-8de8748825b8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42ca4294-13f5-564a-9c61-bfe51e2f5894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42ca4294-13f5-564a-9c61-bfe51e2f5894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300288} :answer-field/id #uuid "af402e53-ece3-5170-871d-14635b65690e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbec592-362f-5cb8-838b-38b868c54f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dbec592-362f-5cb8-838b-38b868c54f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300263} :answer-field/id #uuid "d785ba22-7770-5336-8681-5b6890e427ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9505d474-040a-5e78-97f1-c782cc218ed5" :question/math-academy-id "q-326251" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,},\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | {{field-1}} | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(-3),$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=\\sqrt{\\,t+4\\,}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(-3)=\\sqrt{-3+4}=\\sqrt{1}=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(-1),$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}(-1)^{2}-(-1)=\\frac{3}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $y=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-t.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(2)=\\frac{3}{2}(2)^{2}-(2)=6-2=4.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{5}$ | $\\sqrt{6}$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{33}{2}$ | $8$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503204c2-5202-5eb6-9c99-1d89a4256bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "503204c2-5202-5eb6-9c99-1d89a4256bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300382} :answer-field/id #uuid "775ffea0-6f09-507b-ba4a-f5929a9c5ece" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301596} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20d2ae08-199c-5474-adf2-cfd379ea5346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20d2ae08-199c-5474-adf2-cfd379ea5346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300115} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdb03f8-a8af-5dff-897a-1a48b028739f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8236cfbf-50c1-52a1-9051-6e2573a692b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8236cfbf-50c1-52a1-9051-6e2573a692b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300611} :answer-field/id #uuid "be04d349-7486-598b-9dcd-fc83d123cadf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cefa32c2-7378-5ecb-a3a0-9b87e829889e" :question/math-academy-id "q-326255" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}),\\,y=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}),\\,0\\le t\\le 5.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | {{field-1}} | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{4})=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(3),$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(3)=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi (3)}{6})=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(4),$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi (4)}{6})=sin\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302275 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cda53e7-8da8-5d86-a98c-5728719bc41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cda53e7-8da8-5d86-a98c-5728719bc41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300000} :answer-field/id #uuid "926f273e-d8b0-5e4d-9631-40e611c24ed3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f796a4-f9bc-52c2-95c4-861c28462e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25f796a4-f9bc-52c2-95c4-861c28462e0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300143} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4c15bfd-ddd4-56df-9248-59fef4cfb8ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011fae4e-c40e-5543-bf07-c0c1656584a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299934} :answer-field/id #uuid "da7a0f49-5d74-598d-9cc7-a44f9d26dfa4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301928}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9040c3c-4511-5ef7-a719-36ef3ae85af2" :question/math-academy-id "q-326256" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,y=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-1\\le t\\le 4.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $x(0),$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(0)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (0)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $y(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\ny(1)=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{3})=tan\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $x(2),$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx(2)=cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi (2)}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\nThen the table is \n\n \n\n| **$t$** | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $y$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335928 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054e45cb-ef1a-592f-8ce5-2215be471cc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333032} {:answer/id #uuid "79eda04b-781c-5fda-aa4a-bb2479352bdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334085} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6d0cbe-1f59-57f6-aefd-5d53e15a7b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334353} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb2865c-3deb-55d1-a152-eed996480e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7b9a71e-ffbd-5091-8899-773c38323464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334599} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd68d1f-2e2e-53b3-8c88-e40a6b095d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335680}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9a5f727-046e-5c6d-b3a8-b57aa0e0de57" :question/math-academy-id "q-6742" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=t+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-6,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $b$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=(-3)^{2}-6=9-6=3.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y={t}^{2}-6.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb={0}^{2}-6=0-6=-6.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=3-(-6)-4=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335959 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06ea7064-8984-5ac6-91ea-ed8921bbc138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333056} {:answer/id #uuid "827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f91035-840a-59fe-a14a-8ded740896f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334736} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a7c0bf-869c-5788-8888-00b2ca3dcdac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334846} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2e747f-c905-58fc-9adb-fb9c26ba7608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "827b89fe-a572-54cd-b9cb-dcc0569b217e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334153} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a546347-737e-5d85-bf73-af24c4b5c1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335386}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f35c183e-5200-5f54-ad21-69984c940bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-6825" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=3t-2,\\,\\,\\,y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-8$ | $-5$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $b$ | $5$ | $10$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(-3)-2=-9-2=-11.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into $y=\\frac{10}{{t}^{2}+1}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\frac{10}{(-2)^{2}+1}=\\frac{10}{5}=2.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $x=3t-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=3(3)-2=9-2=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-11+2+7=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} {:answer/id #uuid "1675a734-ba42-53ad-bacc-d3d9a7ecfb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333190} {:answer/id #uuid "379b5cc9-a398-5f20-b13a-5820843260de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333501} {:answer/id #uuid "4e027385-3e35-564e-88cf-8f5955ad0320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333708} {:answer/id #uuid "bbabf68e-a37c-54df-b8af-32120f8b5dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06475ed3-8f81-5f2a-92d7-37b61ba3d841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333047} :answer-field/id #uuid "be306b92-cfe4-5ecc-9451-b14d1a1a3e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335589}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc1d2bf2-3dfe-5506-8434-072c2dc13cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-69922" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=2t+1,\\,\\,\\,y=2t-1,\\,0\\le t\\le 5,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $b$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $c$ | $9$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=2(0)-1=0-1=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=2t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=2(2)+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=2(4)-1=8-1=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=-1-5-7=-13.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Table of Values for a Parametric Curve"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087721 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087522 :question/id #uuid "b322617c-ab21-5ce8-997f-2f10813b4280" :question/math-academy-id "e-5098" :question/problem "Plot the graph of the parametrically defined curve\n\n$$\nx=t(t-6), \\,\\,\\, y=t^3, \\quad -2\\leq t \\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t(t-6).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t^3.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ | $-8$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $8$ |\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/f1/f15f25af0c4804dc811a0ab231ba2ef3ecce2ecd12501a1f2d8b9e34b71a505b.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0dc11d5-8eda-52b1-b7b1-42b481813ff4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049072 :topic/math-academy-id 802 :topic/title "The Domain of a Function"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028939eb-f0d5-530d-bc70-d652b3686217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33a2ed3d605cdd838a5a4b96c04463964c491c08d8bfdb42dc0a9bd815f857a5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278606} {:answer/id #uuid "2b33b70c-a03f-5ef6-9e49-31d44a8a92be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/84c5e6aaa9dfc0312f2a15ed24ce3326f0c811513d3fac22d558bf233fd1b5dc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278974} {:answer/id #uuid "932c9836-8676-515c-96ae-9b00fd239c53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/ac89c944c76160bd9bf67fc48af09d79ddb0092c9a514281c80eec38a3532282.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279900} {:answer/id #uuid "e81996bf-0802-5d8d-8594-a2ce1683b434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b07c61949971bd6279cd325da58